cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "edgeinfer: declared latency, memory and power budgets for aerospace edge inference"
abstract: >-
  edgeinfer treats a deployment envelope for an edge inference computer --
  worst-case latency, median latency, peak memory, a power ceiling and a duty
  cycle -- as a declared, first-class object, and checks a candidate model
  against it two ways: an analytic estimate computed from the model graph with
  nothing executed (operation counts, memory traffic, a roofline latency bound
  and peak memory by liveness analysis) and a measured profile from a real
  onnxruntime session. Worst-case and median latency are reported separately
  throughout, every number carries its measurement method, repeat count and
  combined standard uncertainty, and a verdict whose margin is below the
  measurement uncertainty is reported as marginal. A learned latency predictor
  is benchmarked against the analytic baseline on held-out models over several
  independent measurement passes, and the outcome is reported whichever way it
  falls. Research-grade software; validation level 3, hardware-pending. No
  measurement from an edge target exists.
